# Model ↔ part linking

## Appliance Parts (`parts` table)

- **Source of truth:** `model_parts` (`model_id`, `part_id`, `variation`).
- Use Eloquent `Part::models()` / `Model::parts()` (belongsToMany through `model_parts`).
- **`parts.model_compatibility` is deprecated.** Do not use it to load, filter, or decide which models a part belongs to. It may still be refreshed as a denormalized cache on sync, but it is not authoritative and is often empty for imported WCI data.

## Kit Parts (`kit_catalog_parts` table)

- Kit parts are a **separate catalog**. They do **not** use `model_parts`.
- They still store compatibility as a comma-separated string on `kit_catalog_parts.model_compatibility`.
- Kit Parts has its **own** form partial (`admin/kit-parts/partials/form`). Do **not** include `admin/parts/partials/form` from kit-parts — that form assumes `Part::models()`.

## When changing this area

- Prefer extending `model_parts` / relations for appliance parts.
- Do not "fix" kit-parts by adding `models()` on `KitCatalogPart` unless you also add a real kit-part↔model pivot.
